    "version": "0.21.1",
    "tag": "v0.21.1-beta.1",
    "name": "Coding mode works on Windows",
    "date": "2026-09-25",
    "url": "https://github.com/timetorepo/researchengine/releases/tag/v0.21.1-beta.1",
    "summary": "`` 500 Cannot read properties of null (reading 'name') ``",
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "What you hit",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "On Windows abs is C:\\Users\\…\\projects\\dev-test-k63x and the root is C:\\Users\\…\\projects — so the comparison was false for every project. The IDE considered every project folder invalid."
          },
          {
            "text": "I could not reproduce it on Linux because the check is correct on Linux; it is a Windows-only defect, and the win-x64 build was never run on Windows. That is the actual mistake, and it is now covered by tests that do not need a Windows machine."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The fix",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "isWithinDir / isStrictlyWithinDir",
            "text": "in backend/src/preview/paths.ts: relative() first (the platform-correct test), then a separator- and case-aware prefix fallback so a path built with the other platform's separator still resolves."
          },
          {
            "text": "Used by projectDirOf / projectDirFor, the IDE's safeRel, the Files route's safePath, and the preview's static server."
          },
          {
            "label": "POST /ide/projects no longer depends on a path helper returning a valu…",
            "text": "the name is normalised to a single path segment and joined to the root directly, so no name can produce a null dereference again, on any platform."
          },
          {
            "label": "Python previews work on Windows",
            "text": "python3 does not exist there, so the plan now resolves python3 → python → py, and falls back to the static file server if no interpreter is installed instead of failing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The report got better too",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Platform, everywhere",
            "text": "/api/health reports platform, arch, node and the path separator; the report prints your browser/OS and the server's platform; the Environment panel shows both."
          },
          {
            "label": "The real payload",
            "text": "the Request line shows the actual file map with sizes, not just a list of names."
          },
          {
            "text": "source: — (portable build has no source tree) instead of a bare ?, and the verdict reads PASSED/FAILED — send this report."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Verify",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Download research-engine-0.21.1-beta.1-win-x64.zip, run research-engine.cmd serve, open Coding, and press Try a sample app. On this build the create path returns {ok: true, name: \"sample-landing-…\"} — and Settings → Developer → Test: create a project will say PASSED with your platform in the report."
          },
          {
            "label": "Hashes",
            "text": "(downloads/SHA256SUMS):"
          },
          {
            "text": "`` 702cf9aec57749d0d422ef71929aa482d07b562ecad2b096a0c5c5e2f6cb9ee3 research-engine-0.21.1-beta.1-linux-x64.tar.gz 03fa64325bb935a12b1d11164b4720d883d0fa5d8190c064203cb0d4f5e93966 research-engine-0.21.1-beta.1-win-x64.zip ``"
          },
          {
            "text": "Everything from 0.21 is unchanged: the dock, Sonner wearing the app's toast surface, the shield and morphing focus timer in the top bar, Settings → Developer, and the design sources in docs/design-sources.md."
          },
          {
            "label": "Suites:",
            "text": "render-check 199 (14 of them new for Windows paths), ui-test 60, smoke 65, sample-test 33, design-test 32, engine + workflow suites, both typechecks."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "counts": {
      "items": 14,
      "sections": 4
    }
